# .gitignore — nanosoc-ethernet-chiplet
#
# Grouped by what PRODUCES the file. Two rules of thumb when adding to it:
#
#  * Anchor with a leading `/` only when the path is genuinely fixed. Cadence and
#    Synopsys tools log relative to the directory they were LAUNCHED from, so an
#    anchored rule just means the same droppings reappear elsewhere next week.
#  * A `#` is a comment only at the START of a line. A pattern with a trailing
#    comment silently stops matching, so every comment here is on its own line.
#
# Anything under ci/fixtures/ is hand-written evidence, not tool output; see the
# RE-INCLUDED section at the foot of this file before adding a broad rule.

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.venv/

# ── Editors, merge backups ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.orig

# ── VCS / Verdi / SystemVerilog simulation ──────────────────────────────────
# Waveforms, the compiled binary and its object trees, and the per-run scratch
# VCS drops beside whatever directory it was invoked in.
*.vcd
*.vpd
csrc/
simv
simv.daidir/
sim_build/
ucli.key
vc_hdrs.h
results.xml
results_*.xml
verif/*/*.log
verif/*/csrc/
verif/*/simv_*
verif/*/simv_*.daidir/
verif/*/ucli.key
verif/cdc/build/
verif/elab_strict/build/
# Synopsys vlogan analysis database.
/AN.DB/
# Cocotb generates the per-node DUT filelists from the Makefile.
cocotb/*/dut_src_*.f

# ── Xcelium / HAL lint ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Work library written to the repo root by verif/lint/full/hal_lint.sh; the
# hal.* reports are emitted beside wherever HAL was launched.
/xcelium.d/
hal.design_facts
hal.log
hal.rpt

# ── Synopsys VC Static (vcst) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing in this repo invokes vcst, so these only ever arrive from an ad-hoc
# probe, in whatever directory it ran. Unanchored for that reason.
.vcstPref
vcst_session.log

# ── Cadence Genus / Innovus ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `log*` covers three families deliberately: the plain log, the VERBOSE log
# Innovus writes alongside it (innovus.logv is a distinct file, not a typo), and
# the rotation suffixes both take on re-runs (innovus.log1, genus.log1, ...).
# Unanchored: a stray `genus -batch` or `innovus -files probe.tcl` drops these
# into any directory, including ones that also hold hand-written .tcl.
genus.log*
genus.cmd*
innovus.log*
innovus.cmd*
# Per-iteration run directories, ~2-3 GB each and self-describing: config/ holds
# a copy of every script and constraint used, reproducible from the git SHA in
# MANIFEST.txt.
ASIC/genus-innovus/runs/
ASIC/genus-innovus/baseline_*/
# Full copies of logs/outputs/reports/work taken as a P&R baseline to diff
# against (scripts/ci/asic_stage_report.sh BASELINE_DIR). ~2.7 GB each, and they
# nest one level below where the ASIC/*/{logs,work} rules can reach.
ASIC/*/baseline_*/
# Standard per-stage output trees.
ASIC/*/logs
ASIC/*/outputs
ASIC/*/reports
ASIC/*/work
# ASIC/*/work matches only the literal `work`, so ad-hoc probe sandboxes
# (work_pgprobe/, work_probe/, ...) need their own rule.
ASIC/*/work_*/
# Innovus console capture from the hold experiments. The .tcl beside them is the
# reproducible input and IS tracked; the .out is only stdout.
ASIC/*/holdexp/*.out

# ── Cadence Voltus (rail / IR drop) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Unanchored for the same reason as Genus/Innovus: even `voltus -h` writes a
# voltus.logv into the directory it was launched from.
voltus.log*
voltus.cmd*
# One level deeper than ASIC/*/work, so that rule does NOT cover it. Holds
# power-grid libraries and a pg_capacity report that prints DCCURRENTDENSITY
# limits read straight out of the vendor tech LEF. Those are foundry rule values
# and must not reach a public repository; the scripts and frozen inputs beside
# it are ours and stay tracked.
ASIC/genus-innovus/rail/work/

# ── Calibre / Mentor LVS+DRC, Synopsys IC Validator ─────────────────────────
ASIC/*/calibre_runs
ASIC/imec_results
# v2lvs netlist-translation log, written wherever the LVS flow is invoked from;
# one run of it reached 86 MB. The flow that produces it (ASIC/lvs-flow) IS
# tracked.
v2lvs.log
# IC Validator licence/session droppings.
.icv.*

# ── Cadence Conformal LEC ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# run_lec.sh is pointed at these sandboxes via its *_DIR knobs, so each is a full
# copy of scripts/ + inputs/ plus netlists and reports. These SHADOW the real
# flow scripts: never edit a script inside one, the edit is silently lost.
ASIC/*/lec_*shadow/
/ASIC/eth-chiplet/fv_map_*_gatev_db/
/ASIC/eth-chiplet/hier_tmp*.lec.do

# ── Signoff STA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/ASIC/sta/reports_baseline_*/

# ── Xilinx Vivado / HAPS FPGA prototype ─────────────────────────────────────
.Xil/
vivado*.jou
vivado*.log
vivado*.str
# Vivado implementation run state (.db .sdb .o .so).
/imp/
# BUILD OUTPUTS ONLY. These rules were once /fpga/haps-sx/ and /fpga/haps-sx-pc/,
# which also swallowed ~230 KB of hand-written source (board top, .cob,
# constraints, build scripts). Git cannot re-include a path under an excluded
# directory, so a negation would not have worked — the build dirs must be named
# directly.
/fpga/haps-sx/build/
/fpga/haps-sx-pc/build/

# ── Vendor collateral that must never be committed ──────────────────────────
# This repository is PUBLIC and the TSMC IO-driver LEF is foundry collateral
# whose licence does not permit reproduction. What is committed is the TRANSFORM
# (ASIC/tech_wrappers/tsmc65/scripts/patch_pad_lef.py), never its result.
# scripts/ci/check_no_vendor_collateral.sh fails if a vendor-sized copy reappears
# anywhere tracked; these rules are the first line of that defence, not the only.
ASIC/tech_wrappers/tsmc65/generated/
# local_overrides/ holds a COMPATIBILITY SYMLINK back into generated/. It is not
# cosmetic: a saved Innovus database populates its libs/lef/ with ABSOLUTE
# symlinks into the project tree, and archived databases under
# ASIC/genus-innovus/runs/ and ASIC/eth-chiplet/build/ point at the old path.
# Delete it and read_db aborts with IMPIMEX-7023 on every one of them. The
# symlink adds no vendor bytes to the index because it resolves into generated/.
ASIC/tech_wrappers/tsmc65/local_overrides/*.lef
ASIC/tech_wrappers/tsmc65/local_overrides/*.map
# Mask-ROM libraries built from firmware at flow time.
ASIC/romlibs
# Private commercial letter to the foundry: it must state exact library revisions
# per the mini@sic submission requirements, which is precisely the inventory that
# is not ours to publish. Written here, sent from here, never tracked.
docs/tapeout/27-broker-questions-SEND-NOW.md

# ── This project's build and scratch trees ──────────────────────────────────
build/
build_soc/
scratchpad/
# MkDocs render output.
site/
# Stray stderr capture at the root. Anchored, unlike the tool-log rules above:
# "err.txt" is an ordinary name for a test fixture somewhere under verif/.
/err.txt
# Scratch console captures at the REPO ROOT only. Every real flow logs into
# ASIC/*/logs, verif/*/ or work/. ANCHORED deliberately — a bare `*.log` would
# shadow verif/*/*.log and every other .log rule here, and would swallow any .log
# a test fixture legitimately carries. Zero .log files are tracked today.
/*.log

# ── Claude Code session automation ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Agent definitions, workflow scripts and .claude/settings.local.json, which can
# carry machine-specific paths. Track deliberately if a workflow becomes shared.
.claude/

# ── RE-INCLUDED: ci/fixtures is source, not tool output ─────────────────────
# `scripts/ci/signoff.py prove` overlays these partial repo trees onto a sandbox
# to show each ci/signoff.yaml `check:` can both accept and reject evidence. A
# fixture MUST sit at the path its check really reads, so fixtures legitimately
# appear at generated-looking paths and get caught by the rules above. They are
# hand-written excerpts of a few hundred bytes; no tool wrote any of them.
#
# These negations must stay BELOW the rules they override — last match wins.
#
# This failure mode is quiet in the direction that matters: the fixtures exist on
# the author's disk, `prove` is green locally, and a fresh clone — which is what
# CI is — has none of them, so `prove` reports NO FIXTURE and the gate is
# unproven on the only machine whose verdict counts.
#
# Three checks read into a directory called `build/` (rom-content and rom-gds
# under build/rom_verify/, elab-strict under verif/elab_strict/build/). The
# negation names the DIRECTORY, not the files in it: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so `!.../build/rom_verify/eth.json` would re-include
# nothing — the same trap the /fpga/haps-sx/ comment records.
!/ci/fixtures/**/build/
# `results.xml` and `results_*.xml` above carry no slash, so they match AT ANY
# DEPTH — and the regress fixtures are cocotb result files by definition. Here
# the excluded thing is a FILENAME rather than a directory, so git does descend
# and a file-level negation does re-include.
!/ci/fixtures/**/results.xml
!/ci/fixtures/**/results_*.xml
